= Open science =

== Overview ==
'''Open science''' is a broad set of practices and infrastructures intended to make scientific knowledge, tools, methods, data, and processes more accessible, transparent, reusable, collaborative, and participatory where appropriate.

Open science can include open access, open data, open-source research software, open methods, preprints, open educational resources, open infrastructures, and wider participation in knowledge creation and evaluation.

Openness is not absolute: ethical, legal, privacy, security, cultural, and technical constraints can legitimately limit access to particular research objects.

== Boundaries ==
* open science ≠ open access only
* open science ≠ all research must be public without limits
* openness ≠ reproducibility automatically

